//? Title: General Problem Solver: finite facts, executable plans and safe depth limits
//? Subtitle: Actual forward-search events, a corrected pruning counterexample and independently checked plans
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find a sequence of applicable actions that changes an initial set of facts into
a state satisfying a goal, while limiting the number of actions. Search can
branch, revisit states and spend its step budget on an unproductive route.
Datamunge’s General Problem Solver API represents facts as 64-bit masks and
searches in operator order. This report starts with the original one-action
example, checks a key-and-door plan independently and explains why a state reached
with more remaining budget must be reopened. A binary-counter family measures
actual exponential search work, while explicit record and certificate limits
make the ownership and resource contracts visible.
)

\toc

> Start with the original one-action problem

Initially fact 0 is false. The goal requires it, and an always-applicable operator
named make adds it. There is one selected action and the terminal mask is 1.
The native trace records six control-flow events: visit the root, test the
operator, apply it, visit the successor, accept the goal, then propagate success.
The original program merely returned exit status 0; the executed table below makes
the same successful result inspectable.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/planner_first.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/general_problem_solver.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<dm::algorithms::PlanningAction>a{{"make",0,1,0}};
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_trace(0,1,a,32,6);const auto legacy=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver(0,1,a);
 std::print("| event | state | depth | next state |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(const auto&e:t.events)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",dm::algorithms::planning_event_name(e.kind),e.state,e.depth,e.next_state);
 std::print("\nFound {}; action {}; index {}; final mask {}; visits {}; checks {}; records {}; legacy result identical {}.\n",t.run.result.found,t.run.result.actions.at(0),t.run.action_indices.at(0),t.run.result.final_state,t.run.work.visits,t.run.work.operator_checks,t.events.size(),legacy.actions==t.run.result.actions&&legacy.final_state==t.run.result.final_state);
 const auto applied=std::find_if(t.events.begin(),t.events.end(),[](const auto&e){return e.kind==dm::algorithms::PlanningEventKind::apply;});
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(63,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.2;box.height=2.2;box.font_size=22;
 d.node("start",{0,0},std::format("Initial facts\nmask = {}\ngoal bit absent",applied->state),box)
  .node("action",{5.8,0},std::format("Operator {}: {}\nrequires {}\nadds {}, removes {}",applied->action_index,a[0].name,a[0].require,a[0].add,a[0].remove),box)
  .node("goal",{11.6,0},std::format("Actual successor\nmask = {}\ngoal bit present",applied->next_state),box)
  .edge("start","action","applicable").edge("action","goal","apply effects")
  .text({5.8,2.5},"Planning changes the model; it does not execute an external action",24).save_svg("build/planner_first.svg");
 if(!legacy.found||t.events.size()!=6||t.run.action_indices!=std::vector<std::size_t>{0})throw std::runtime_error("original make plan");
}
