> A finite fact model is smaller than historical GPS or full STRIPS

A mask s encodes a set of currently true facts. Every bit, including bit 63, is
available. An operator has positive preconditions R, added facts A and deleted
facts D. A goal mask G is a conjunction: every set bit must hold, while other
facts may remain present. The transition rules are

$$
\operatorname{applicable}(s,R)\iff(s\mathbin{\&}R)=R,
\qquad s'=(s\mathbin{\&}\mathord{\sim}D)\mathbin{|}A,
\qquad\operatorname{goal}(s,G)\iff(s\mathbin{\&}G)=G.
$$
\alttext(An operator is applicable when all required bits are present; clear its deletion bits then set its addition bits; success means all positive goal bits are present.)

Deletion precedes addition, so an overlapping effect ends present. An empty
precondition is always satisfied, and a zero goal succeeds initially. There are
no negative preconditions, logical variables or hidden consistency constraints:
if two fact bits ought to be mutually exclusive, the supplied effects must enforce
that model. Operator names are labels; positions in the input vector identify
actions even when labels are empty or duplicated.

[Fikes and Nilsson’s original STRIPS paper, IJCAI 1971, pages 608–619](https://ijcai.org/proceedings/1971/63),
Section II.A–B, describes preconditions and add/delete effects in a richer
first-order model. It also uses goal differences to select relevant operators
and generate subgoals. This library adapts grounded fact effects but uses ordinary
forward DFS in input order. Its historical API name does not imply an implementation
of original GPS means–ends reasoning or a first-order theorem prover. The
[original paper, printed 609](https://ijcai.org/proceedings/1971/0063.pdf)
makes that distinction clear. Here an operator application changes a state mask;
no robot, file, network or other external action is executed.

> Check a key-and-door plan independently

Use bit 0 for holding a key, bit 1 for an unlocked door and bit 2 for being inside.
Getting a key adds bit 0. Unlocking requires the key, deletes that key bit and
adds the unlocked bit. Entering requires the unlocked bit and adds the inside
bit. The input list is ordered enter, unlock, get-key, so forward search tests
unavailable actions before finding the first applicable one. This ordering is
explicit; no goal-relevance heuristic rearranges it.

The native checker executes the returned operator indices independently of the
search and retains every reached prefix state. It verifies applicability and
goal satisfaction; it does not certify shortestness or impose a step budget.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/planner_door.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/general_problem_solver.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<dm::algorithms::PlanningAction>a{{"enter",2,4,0},{"unlock",1,2,1},{"get-key",0,1,0}};
 const auto r=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_run(0,4,a,3);const auto c=dm::algorithms::check_planning_plan(0,4,a,r.action_indices,4);
 std::print("| step | operator index | action | state before | state after |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t k=0;k<r.action_indices.size();++k){const auto i=r.action_indices[k];std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k+1,i,a[i].name,c.states[k],c.states[k+1]);}
 const auto bad=dm::algorithms::check_planning_plan(0,4,a,{0},2);
 std::print("\nPlan applicable {}; reaches goals {}; final mask {}; applications {}; search checks {}; unavailable-enter certificate applicable {}; its retained states {}.\n",c.applicable,c.reaches_goals,c.final_state,c.applied,r.work.operator_checks,bad.applicable,bad.states.size());
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(58,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.1;box.height=2.1;box.font_size=22;
 const std::array<std::string,4>labels{"No key\nDoor locked","Key present\nDoor locked","Key consumed\nDoor unlocked","Inside\nDoor unlocked"};
 for(std::size_t k=0;k<c.states.size();++k){const auto id=std::to_string(k);d.node(id,{double(k)*4.4,0},std::format("{}\nmask = {}",labels[k],c.states[k]),box);if(k)d.edge(std::to_string(k-1),id,a[r.action_indices[k-1]].name);}
 d.text({6.6,2.4},"Independent certificate: every selected operator must be applicable",25).save_svg("build/planner_door.svg");
 if(!r.result.found||!c.applicable||!c.reaches_goals||c.states!=std::vector<std::uint64_t>{0,1,2,6}||bad.applicable)throw std::runtime_error("independent door certificate");
}
