> Why a global visited set can break a depth-limited search

A repeated state may be reached at a different depth. If the first route uses
two of three available steps and a later route uses only one, the later route
has more remaining budget. Rejecting it solely because the mask was seen can
lose a valid bounded plan.

The following three-operator example was reduced from an independently verified
counterexample found during this conversion. Start at mask 4, require goal bits 3,
and allow at most three actions. clear removes bit 2; set adds bits 1 and 2 and
removes bit 1 first; consume requires bit 1, deletes the three low bits and adds
bit 0. Add-wins makes set’s bit 1 present after its overlapping effects.

Input order first explores clear, then set: state 4→0→6 reaches 6 at depth 2.
That branch cannot finish in its one remaining step. Later, set directly gives
state 4→6 at depth 1. Reopening it exposes the valid path 4→6→1→7, using
set, consume, set. The old state-only visited implementation incorrectly returned
failure at budget 3. The corrected implementation records the smallest expansion
depth of each state and reopens only at a strictly smaller depth.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/planner_reopen.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/general_problem_solver.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<dm::algorithms::PlanningAction>a{{"clear",0,0,4},{"set",0,6,2},{"consume",2,1,7}};
 std::print("| maximum steps | found | selected length | reopenings | operator checks |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(std::size_t budget=0;budget<=6;++budget){const auto r=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_run(4,3,a,budget);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",budget,r.result.found,r.action_indices.size(),r.work.reopenings,r.work.operator_checks);}
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_trace(4,3,a,3,0);const auto c=dm::algorithms::check_planning_plan(4,3,a,t.run.action_indices,4);
 const auto e=std::find_if(t.events.begin(),t.events.end(),[](const auto&e){return e.kind==dm::algorithms::PlanningEventKind::reopen&&e.state==6&&e.depth==1;});if(e==t.events.end())throw std::runtime_error("missing actual reopen");
 std::print("\nActual reopened mask {}; previous depth {}; new depth {}; previous remaining budget {}; new remaining budget {}.\n",e->state,e->previous_depth,e->depth,3-e->previous_depth,3-e->depth);
 std::print("Certified plan indices ({}, {}, {}); states ({}, {}, {}, {}); final goals satisfied {}.\n",t.run.action_indices[0],t.run.action_indices[1],t.run.action_indices[2],c.states[0],c.states[1],c.states[2],c.states[3],c.reaches_goals);
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(64,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.2;box.height=2.3;box.font_size=22;
 d.node("deep",{0,0},std::format("First expanded mask {}\ndepth = {}\n{} step remaining",e->state,e->previous_depth,3-e->previous_depth),box)
  .node("shallow",{5.9,0},std::format("Later arrival, mask {}\ndepth = {}\n{} steps remaining",e->state,e->depth,3-e->depth),box)
  .node("goal",{11.8,0},std::format("Independent certificate\n{} -> {} -> {}\ngoal satisfied",c.states[1],c.states[2],c.states[3]),box)
  .edge("deep","shallow","reopen").edge("shallow","goal","consume, set")
  .text({5.9,2.5},"The same state with more remaining steps is a stronger search opportunity",24).save_svg("build/planner_reopen.svg");
 if(!t.run.result.found||!c.applicable||!c.reaches_goals||c.states!=std::vector<std::uint64_t>{4,6,1,7})throw std::runtime_error("corrected bounded plan");
}
