Largest checked prefix states 32769; independent goal certificate true; the search uses heap frames rather than recursive C++ calls.
\image(figures/planner_scaling.svg)
// result_end
\caption(At 16 bits, the actual selected plan has 32768 actions and the heap stack reaches 32769 frames. These are executed counts and independently checked states, not a wall-clock benchmark.)
\alttext(Log-base-two selected plan length and node visits rise linearly with the number of input bits, demonstrating exponential counts. The table shows exact checks, repeat prunes, cutoffs and heap-stack size through 16 bits.)

With m operators and S reachable states, each expanded state can be reopened
only at a strictly smaller depth. A cycle cannot improve the depth of an active
ancestor, so stored depths are below both K+1 and S. This gives an expected bound
of O(m S min(K+1,S)) precondition checks with constant-width bit operations and
expected constant-time hashing. Ordinary working storage is O(S+min(K,S)) frame/map
records, plus the returned operator indices and copied name bytes. S itself can
be exponential in the number of facts. No table for all 2^64 possible masks is
preallocated, and replacing recursion with heap frames does not make exponential
search cheap.

> Online event records and whole certificate states are different quotas

Search history size is unknown before exploring the domain. The trace therefore
checks each actual next event against an online cap: default one million records,
zero disables only that optional quota. One record has the fixed PlanningEvent
schema; it is not one numeric entry or byte. Owned input operators and their
names, root/work metadata, final ordinary output, working stack/map and allocator
storage are excluded. This is not a peak RAM limit. The final finish records
count too, and exceeding the cap throws without returning a partial trace.

The independent checker knows the proposed sequence length p in advance. It
validates every operator index first, then admits the complete p+1 state bound,
including the initial state, before performing any transition or allocating its
history. A precondition failure can leave a shorter valid prefix, but receives
no early-failure quota discount. It reports applicability and whether that prefix
satisfies the goal separately. A true goal flag alone does not make a sequence
with a failed action applicable.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/planner_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/general_problem_solver.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<dm::algorithms::PlanningAction>make{{"make",0,1,0}};const auto observed=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_trace(0,1,make,32,0);bool event_denied=false;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_trace(0,1,make,32,5);}catch(const std::length_error&){event_denied=true;}
 auto t=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_trace(0,1,make,32,6);t.operators[0].name="mutated";t.events[2].next_state=999;const bool owned=t.run.result.actions[0]=="make"&&t.run.result.final_state==1&&t.events[3].state==1;
 const auto high=std::uint64_t{1}<<63;const std::vector<dm::algorithms::PlanningAction>a{{"same",0,high,high},{"same",high,1,high}};const auto r=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_run(0,1,a,2);const auto c=dm::algorithms::check_planning_plan(0,1,a,r.action_indices,3);
 bool certificate_denied=false,index_first=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::check_planning_plan(0,1,a,r.action_indices,2);}catch(const std::length_error&){certificate_denied=true;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::check_planning_plan(0,1,a,{999},1);}catch(const std::out_of_range&){index_first=true;}
 const auto failed=dm::algorithms::check_planning_plan(0,1,a,{1},2);const auto initial=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_trace(high,high,{},0,2);const auto zero=dm::algorithms::general_problem_solver_trace(0,1,make,0,2);
 std::print("| resource | observed or required | admitted or captured | rejected cap | rejection observed |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Actual search-event records | {} | {} | 5 | {} |\n| Whole certificate states | {} | {} | 2 | {} |\n",observed.events.size(),t.events.size(),event_denied,r.action_indices.size()+1,c.states.size(),certificate_denied);
 std::print("\nDuplicate names {}; certified indices ({}, {}); high-bit prefix states ({:#018x}, {:#018x}, {:#018x}); applicable {}; goals reached {}.\n",a[0].name==a[1].name,r.action_indices[0],r.action_indices[1],c.states[0],c.states[1],c.states[2],c.applicable,c.reaches_goals);
 std::print("Independent owned copies {}; index validation before quota {}; invalid-precondition plan applicable {}; retained prefix states {}; initial-goal events {}; zero-budget failure events {}.\n",owned,index_first,failed.applicable,failed.states.size(),initial.events.size(),zero.events.size());
 auto eventplot=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(observed.events.size()),double(t.events.size()),5.},{"Observed","Admitted","Rejected cap"});eventplot.title("Online actual search records").xlab("").ylab("Fixed-schema event records").y_limits(0,8);
 auto certplot=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(r.action_indices.size()+1),double(c.states.size()),2.},{"Required","Captured","Rejected cap"});certplot.title("Whole independent certificate").xlab("").ylab("64-bit prefix states, initial included").y_limits(0,4);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(eventplot).add(certplot).size(1100,500).title("Online event capture and known-length certificate admission").fit_panels().save_svg("build/planner_controls.svg");
 if(!event_denied||!certificate_denied||!index_first||!owned||!c.applicable||!c.reaches_goals||failed.applicable)throw std::runtime_error("record, certificate and identity controls");
}
